# StatusText

> Lede 0.6.0's docs for StatusText, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/status-text.md

A status word colored by its tone, with a dot, at the size of the text around it, for a ListRow's `value`, a table cell or a sentence.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/status-text @lede/list
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md) and [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md). It adds [`list`](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/list.md) only because the example below imports it. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.6.0/status-text.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { StatusText } from '@/components/lede/status-text';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/status-text.tsx` | `@/components/lede/status-text` | `StatusText` (component), `StatusTone` (type, from `tone.ts`), `StatusTextProps` (type) |

## Props

A `<span>` that colors a status word by its tone, with a dot before it. It takes the size of the text around it, so it fits a ListRow's `value` or `subtitle`, a table cell or a sentence.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `children` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  | The status in words, such as "Failed" or "Up to date". The tone only adds color, so the words carry the meaning. |
| `tone` | `StatusTone` | `neutral` | Default `'neutral'`. |
| `dot` | `boolean` | `true` | A dot in the tone's color before the words. Default `true`. |
| `className` | `string` |  |  |

These props use types from other items:

- `StatusTone` is `ToneSubset<'neutral' | 'positive' | 'caution' | 'critical'>`, declared in [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md#types).

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { ListGroup, ListRow } from '@/components/lede/list';
import { StatusText } from '@/components/lede/status-text';

export function DeployChecks() {
  return (
    <ListGroup title="Needs attention" summary="2 of 14 hosts">
      <ListRow title="edge-sfo-2" subtitle="Deploy failed at 9:41 AM" value={<StatusText tone="critical">Failed</StatusText>} href="/hosts/edge-sfo-2" />
      <ListRow title="api-iad-1" subtitle="Plan has 3 changes" value={<StatusText tone="caution">Would change</StatusText>} href="/hosts/api-iad-1" />
    </ListGroup>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

